    "history": "Contiguous complete trailing days, up to14 for primary; 1–6 limited,7–13 provisional,14 full. Diagnostics7/14/30/available60. Daily anchors strictly prior to observation, lag<24h. Zero is valid; missing breaks runs.",
    "episodes": "5m volume / previous daily primary median / F. F is past-only cross-sectional median Q90/Q50. Major spike is consecutive 5m exceedance of B=market median past Q99/Q50; hour active if median12 ratios>1 with all valid. Unknown hours break quiet. First left-boundary episode may be censored.",
    "categories_rule": "Persistent high: Q10>market median usual volume ×F. Noisy: >=1 5m spike episode/day, unless high-floor (separate noisy flag retained). Dormant: >=7 quiet days, <1 spike/day, usual volume<=market reference×F. Moderate otherwise. Requires>=7d; no names or future returns. Descriptive units, not natural clusters.",
    "fading": "Recent half-window Q75 < older half Q25. Trend7/14/30 = median newer half / older half. Reviving = six closed5m candles above their causal threshold. Quiet_share is observed quiet hour fraction, not a weighted or calibrated dormancy score.",
    "limitations": "Daily state can lag<24h; turnover not orderbook depth/trade count. No universal0–100 composite: axes depend on history and are correlated. Later period is temporal check on already-known data, not independent validation."
  },
